# Environment contract — NAMES ONLY, NEVER VALUES.
#
# This is the `main` branch template. A project's own branch replaces <PROJECT> with its
# prefix and lists the variables that project actually reads.
#
# Copy to .env locally. Every variable here is documented with a verification step in
# docs/env-matrix.md. The app FAILS TO START when a required one is missing — that is
# deliberate; a silent default is how a prod outage starts.
#
# Use CHANGE_ME_LOCAL_ONLY as the placeholder. Never a realistic-looking fake: it gets
# copied into production by someone in a hurry.

# --- Database: managed Postgres via the SESSION pooler (port 5432, NOT 6543) ------------
# Three traps, all of which fail confusingly — see docs/env-matrix.md:
#   1. Direct connections are often IPv6-only; the error looks like a firewall problem.
#   2. Transaction mode (6543) has no prepared statements, which ORMs and migration
#      tools both need. Same host, different port, different semantics.
#   3. A migration tool's advisory lock is connection-scoped, so transaction pooling can
#      release it on a different backend than took it.
# The provider hands you a libpq URL; a JVM app needs a JDBC one. Prepend `jdbc:` and
# drop any embedded user:password@.
<PROJECT>_DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://<host>.pooler.example.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
<PROJECT>_DB_USERNAME=postgres.<project-ref>
<PROJECT>_DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_LOCAL_ONLY
# Sized against the DATABASE's connection limit, not expected load.
<PROJECT>_DB_POOL_MAX=5

# --- Identity ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The backend verifies tokens and never issues them. No password, no session, no token
# minting anywhere. The project id is NOT a secret.
<PROJECT>_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=

# --- Runtime ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
<PROJECT>_PORT=8080
<PROJECT>_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Origin only. No trailing slash, no path.
<PROJECT>_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://<your-service>.onrender.com

# --- NOT env vars -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything governing SPEND, PRICING or a LIMIT lives in the app_config table so it can be
# changed during an incident without a deploy. A project's branch lists its own keys here.
